<p>Norwegian police arrested three brothers — Norwegian citizens of Iraqi origin — on suspicion of carrying out a “terrorist bombing” after an explosion outside the US embassy in Oslo over the weekend. Authorities said the blast caused minor damage and no one was hurt. Police prosecutor Christian Hatlo said investigators are still weighing several possible motives, including whether the attack was ordered by a government entity — given the target and the wider global security situation. Police believe one brother placed the bomb and the other two were complicit, and they have not ruled out ties to criminal networks. Iran’s ambassador in Oslo denied any involvement in the Oslo explosion and said it was unacceptable for Iran to be singled out.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/riANgQHfoZkMeZDUwYZTIipAltr-DmDu2HaqdSDQhA0d1Be8qP_a89watWGv0j8ODFXovdsunDPNJzVokUed7RW_BFL8W8HftSWnHfDM_kbs' alt='Police vehicles outside the U.S. embassy, after a loud bang was reported at the site, in Oslo, Norway, March 8, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Suspects’ profile: Hatlo said the brothers are in their 20s and were not previously known to police.</li><li>Arrest timing: Hatlo said police arrested the brothers in Oslo around 3:30pm local time (2:30pm GMT).</li><li>Investigation focus: Hatlo said investigators are still working to pin down the roles each brother played.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Norwegian police (Christian Hatlo): Investigators are pursuing multiple motive hypotheses, including possible direction by a government entity, and are also considering potential ties to criminal networks. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-embassy-explosion-norway-oslo-arrests/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Iran’s ambassador in Oslo (Alireza Jahangiri): He denied Iranian involvement in the explosion and said it was unacceptable for Iran to be singled out. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981008/three-brothers-of-iraqi-origin-arrested-over-us-embassy-blast-in-oslo'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Norwegian security service PST: In its annual threat assessment, PST warned that Iran could use “proxy actors,” including criminal networks, to commit acts. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981008/three-brothers-of-iraqi-origin-arrested-over-us-embassy-blast-in-oslo'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981008/three-brothers-of-iraqi-origin-arrested-over-us-embassy-blast-in-oslo'>Three brothers of Iraqi origin arrested over US embassy blast in Oslo</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3346274/3-brothers-iraq-links-arrested-terrorist-bombing-us-embassy-norway'>3 brothers with Iraq links arrested for ‘terrorist bombing’ of US embassy in Norway</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2grl7lrrmo'>Three brothers arrested after explosion at US embassy in Oslo</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/norway-police-apprehend-three-suspects-in-u-s-embassy-bombing'>Three brothers arrested over US embassy blast in Oslo</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-embassy-explosion-norway-oslo-arrests/'>3 brothers arrested in connection with U.S. embassy explosion in Norway</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/11/three-norwegian-brothers-arrested-us-embassy-blast-oslo'>Three Norwegian brothers arrested over US embassy blast in Oslo</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ctvnews.ca/world/article/three-brothers-arrested-over-us-embassy-blast-in-oslo-police/'>Norwegian police arrest three brothers on suspicion of involvement in a bombing outside the U.S. embassy in Oslo on 8 March that caused minor damage but no injuries. A terrorist motive is suspected.</a> - ctvnews.ca</li></ul>